      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Static portals to specific instances feature was mentioned on 14 September 2023 developer update, but then this segment got removed.\n\nTupper said: \"Static portal segment’s been pulled because apparently it’s not gonna work quite that way. We’ll talk more about it later.\"\n\nI just want to say: please do it the way you described in this segment. It will open up a LOT of possibilities for world creators. Personally I imagine a lot of cool ways to use this combined with remote string loading\n\nDeleted segment itself:\n\nStatic Portal Improvement\n\nSoon, we’ll be improving static portals to allow our creators more control over them!\n\nUsing the portal marker, you can now define an entire worldID:instanceID combo to link to a specific instance, instead of just linking to a random instance of the world. Of course, simply entering a standard wrld_id will still work. All the worlds that already use worldID static portals will continue to work like they always have.\n\nBut now, you have the option of putting in a specific instance! We’ve had a lot of cool ideas how creators might use this – emulating the old “webring” style by instance linking, creating contiguous roleplaying experiences, or even building hubs of “constant instances” where a user might go to find new communities. Combine this with Group instances so you have moderators on hand, and you’ve got a lot of opportunity to build communities in new, interesting ways!\n\nWe’re excited to see how creators employ this tiny change to link together their experiences.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
